<<~ &#x0002; >>

! The Founding Runbook ~ the go-live rite

> A woken operator runs this rite to stand a node fresh-from-void, found the three-kahu
> quorum, arm the charter's pre-rotation, and go live. Each step reads as its own verb; the
> irreversible one wears a warning. The rite runs top to bottom once — a re-run re-founds.

<<~ ahu #the-rite >>

!! The rite ~ rehearsed first, then the six movements, then the growing

<<~loops ⓪ rehearse -> ✶ clear -> ⏿ found -> ◇ reserve -> ▶ seal-and-back-up -> ↺ regenesis -> LIVE -> ⚲ crossroads -> ⊕ grow -> ⊛ gather -> ⊙ feed -> ⊘ dwell >>

''Rehearse'' runs the whole rite in containers, disposably, until it bores (#rehearse) · ''clear''
pares the vessel to void · ''found'' stands the device + the three kahu · ''reserve'' forges the
pre-rotation's future-key custody · ''seal-and-back-up'' locks the secrets at rest + writes a
recoverable copy · ''regenesis'' re-seeds the content from `bags/` · ''LIVE'' serves ·
''crossroads'' stands a Herm where a family needs one (#crossroads) · ''grow'' opens the Nexus,
contracts fellow operators, and welcomes users at the anon floor (#grow-the-nexus) · ''gather'' brings the
operator's own vessels in as contracted leaves (#gather-the-fleet) · ''feed'' lays the first offering, which
IS the realm's founding (#feed-the-realm) · ''dwell'' seats a second operator IN the realm rather than
merely carrying for it (#dwell).

''The last three movements run AFTER LIVE and never gate it'' — and they carry different readiness. ⊛ Gather
runs today on built verbs. ⊙ Feed names an OWED surface over machinery that already stands. ⊘ Dwell holds a
built vouch and a crossing that REFUSES until the operator seats the admission dials — and its conversion act
stays un-modelled by ruling, so no command there may name a quorum, a waiting period, or a test.

''THE RITE RUNS IN TWO BRANCHES, and they want opposite virtues'' (operator ruling, 2026-07-27).
A ''REHEARSAL'' founding runs in containers, disposably, as many times as it takes — cheapness IS
the point and nothing stands worth backing up. A ''KEEPER'' founding runs once, on the real hearth,
irreversibly. ''Movements ②–⑨ read the same in both''; the branches part at ① and at what a failure
COSTS. Every rehearsal therefore doubles as a dress rehearsal of the keeper — same commands, same
order, disposable stakes — which stops the keeper from ever being a first take.

''THE RITE STANDS ONE VESSEL; THE ARC RUNS WIDER.'' What happens across several vessels, several operators and however long the months take — a realm FED after LIVE, a fleet gathered as contracted leaves, a second operator founding independently and then DWELLING IN the first realm — rides at <<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/first-realm-arc >>. It names three stretches this rite does not walk: the fleet join (② names the CONTRACTED mode and walks only SELF-STOOD), the realm feeding (no movement names the first offering, and `feedCabalRealm` stands built and unwalked), and the dwelling join (⊕ Grow contracts CARRIAGE and seats no DWELLER — carriage and dwelling ride orthogonal axes).

''Read this rite as the operator-instruction source.'' Each movement names its branch, its exact
commands, and its precondition, so a reader (human or agent) can answer //what do I run next// from
the vessel's current state rather than from memory (#agent-seed).

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #rehearse >>

!! ⓪ Rehearse ~ run it in a box until it bores (the REHEARSAL branch opens here)

''A ceremony nobody has performed carries no evidence, only intent.'' This rite stood `proposed` and
unrun while the code beneath it moved for a week — so the first movement stands one that costs
nothing to repeat. The harness already stands: `docker-compose.mesh.yml` founds ''real'' identities
in containers (`tools/lararium-container-boot.sh` — //founds its OWN identity, then composeHerm//)
with two Herm relays on a shared network.

```
docker compose -f docker-compose.mesh.yml up --abort-on-container-exit   # found, in a box
tools/herm-mesh-witness.sh                                               # witness the crossroads carry
docker compose -f docker-compose.mesh.yml down -v                        # THE CLEAR — no backup, nothing kept
```

''The burn IS the clear, and that inverts the danger.'' Where the keeper branch opens on the most
destructive command in the house, the rehearsal branch opens on one whose whole virtue reads
//repeatable//. Run it until the sequence bores; ''boredom names the readiness the keeper needs''.

''What a rehearsal proves that a test cannot.'' The suites prove every property in-process, authored
by the same hand that wrote the code — the field has never disagreed. A container founding lets
sockets be rude, disks be real, and a drop actually drop: it stands the cheapest ''outside island''
available (#the-frame). Deliberately in scope here: remote CAS transit to a holder outside this
process, bilateral genesis across two sovereign hearths, the Herm's re-key/re-share/heal teeth, and
reconnection after a real drop.

''FIRST RUN — 2026-07-27, and the rite amends itself as promised.'' Three cycles ran. ''2 green, 1 red.''
What the field said, recorded here because the run outranks the document:

# ''THE RITE'S OWN INSTRUMENTS OVERCLAIMED — twice, and neither failure reaches a test suite.'' The
  cycle runner declared `cycles green: 1/1` while BOTH witnesses failed (a bash `if` without `else`
  yields 0, so the status read the branch and never the command). The carry witness printed
  //verified at each hop// while a hop read UNVERIFIED (its gate checks the LAST hop alone). Both cured;
  the runner now ''proves its own detector'' before trusting a cycle, and refuses to proceed when a
  forced failure fails to register. ''A verdict MUST state its own scope, or a green measures the
  instrument's silence.''
# ''AN INTERMITTENT FAIL-CLOSED BINDING GATE, ~1 cold founding in 3.'' `herm-relay-2` exits 1 with
  //persona-KEL chain for the pinned identifier … absent from the local board replica — the Binding
  Gate cannot reach a head (fail-closed)//. A second identical run stands all four vessels clean. ''A
  RACE, never a structural break'' — precisely the class one test run cannot see and a repeated
  rehearsal does. Surfaced, deliberately undiagnosed: the Binding Gate sits in live work, and
  #found already names this failure shape as the cost of founding without a carried chain.
# ''WHAT PASSED, and it matters.'' On a healthy mesh the announced dial crosses source → relay-1 →
  relay-2 with the pointer signed, the snapshot hash-matched and the dial DECODED; and the partition
  witness confirms relay-2 keeps advancing after the witness CUTS relay-1 — federation riding carried dials,
  never a hardcoded peer list.

''The rite therefore does NOT yet earn `status = live`.'' One movement stands amended (this one), and a
red cycle stands unexplained. ''Boredom has not arrived.''

''The rehearsal amends this meme; this meme does not predict the rehearsal.'' Where a run contradicts
a movement below, ''the run wins'' and the movement gets rewritten — the rite earns `status = live`
only after a rehearsal completes end-to-end without an amendment.

!!! SECOND PASS — 2026-08-04, and the rite amends again without a rehearsal

''A reading against live code found what a run would have found, so the same law applies.'' Three
amendments landed and one hypothesis got recorded:

# ''⓪′ PREFLIGHT ADDED, ahead of the irreversible clear.'' The toolchain went unchecked before a movement
  that cannot be undone. Measured: the entry point died at import on a stale build.
# ''⊛ GATHER'S COMMANDS CONTRADICTED ITS OWN PROSE.'' The text described a joining vessel minting its own
  key and receiving a signed edge — correct. The commands signed a payload before any joinee key existed
  — impossible: the signing call refuses without the joinee's public verifying key. ''The description
  tracked the design and the sequence tracked the past'', which reads as the most dangerous shape a
  runbook carries, because the prose reassures the reader that the commands were checked.
# ''THE ADMIT PAYLOAD'S CONTENTS NAMED.'' It carries one signed edge on a lineage, never a
  capability-event bundle (#gather).
# ''A CANDIDATE FOR THE STANDING RED, unproven.'' The unexplained fail-closed Binding Gate reports a
  persona-KEL chain absent from the local board replica. An admit payload measured 2026-08-04 carries a
  chain of ''length 1''. A one-event chain against an unsynced replica reads as a plausible
  cannot-reach-a-head shape. <<~ confidence Provisional 4/20 >> ''NOT reproduced'' — recorded so the next
  rehearsal watches the chain length, never as a diagnosis.

''The corroboration, with its limit named.'' The founding-then-admit path stands green end-to-end in an
automated witness (9 of 9, 2026-08-04). ''That witness is not this rite'' — it stands no containers, its
sockets stay polite, and no drop actually drops (#rehearse). It corroborates the SHAPE of movements ②
and ⊛; it substitutes for no cycle.

